From 3d5a0a73a89e670d7cbc9914a8ad85e6e5df5db0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: banidu-512 <madmacmester@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 21:48:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] onnx: CUDA 12 on Linux, CUDA and DirectML builds on
 Windows, CPU fallback fixes

Pin ONNX Runtime to 1.24.4, the last release with a DirectML build and a CUDA 12 GPU build (1.28+ needs CUDA 13, which Pascal cards and driver 550 cannot run).
Windows ships the GPU and DirectML natives side by side; OnnxNativeSelector binds one per operator package on first use, switching needs a restart.
Linux probes for the CUDA 12 libraries before appending the CUDA provider and logs what is missing instead of failing inside native code.
The CPU provider uses the extended optimization level: 1.24 cannot initialize the fp16 Depth Anything graph at ENABLE_ALL.
Linux docs describe CUDA 12 and that MediaPipe works.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
